WEBVTT

00:00:05.026 --> 00:00:08.398
<v><b>Max:</b></v> I arrived at Madrid airport where I met Paula.

00:00:09.073 --> 00:00:10.533
<i>Hola, Soy Max.</i>

00:00:10.606 --> 00:00:12.338
<v><b>Paula:</b></v> <i>Encantada. Soy Paula.</i>

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:18.826
<v><b>Max:</b></v> Paula took me to my hotel, and that evening we went to the centre of Madrid

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:21.453
and it was time for my first test.

00:00:21.799 --> 00:00:26.916
I had to order a sandwich and a drink in a bar, then ask for the bill.

00:00:29.668 --> 00:00:34.284
I sat down at the bar and I tried to order a beer and a ham sandwich:

00:00:35.231 --> 00:00:40.296
<i>Por favor, una cerveza y un bocadillo de jamón.</i>

00:00:40.483 --> 00:00:41.283
<v><b>Waiter:</b></v> <i>En seguida</i>.

00:00:41.969 --> 00:00:45.970
<v><b>Max:</b></v> Fantastic! The waiter understood me first time.

00:00:46.501 --> 00:00:51.284
My pronunciation wasn’t perfect, but I got my beer and my sandwich.

00:00:51.717 --> 00:00:52.823
I really enjoyed it.

00:00:53.483 --> 00:00:55.638
But then the more difficult bit.

00:00:56.056 --> 00:00:59.973
Asking for the bill… <i>Cuánto es?</i>

00:01:00.013 --> 00:01:01.019
<v><b>Waiter:</b></v> <i>Seis noventa</i>.

00:01:01.625 --> 00:01:02.091
<v><b>Max:</b></v> <i>¿Cómo?</i>

00:01:02.658 --> 00:01:04.664
<v><b>Waiter:</b></v> <i>Seis noventa</i>.

00:01:05.017 --> 00:01:06.137
<v><b>Max:</b></v> Six ninety.

00:01:06.562 --> 00:01:10.612
I understood! Paula gave me eight points for the test.

00:01:11.043 --> 00:01:12.592
I was very happy with that.

00:01:13.186 --> 00:01:15.812
Next we went out into the street.

00:01:17.141 --> 00:01:23.483
Test number two was asking for directions and (very important!) understanding them.

00:01:24.261 --> 00:01:31.530
We were in a narrow street, and I had to stop someone and ask them for the nearest chemist, <i>una farmacia</i>.

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:33.836
I stopped a woman.

00:01:33.837 --> 00:01:36.740
At first I didn’t understand anything she said!

00:01:37.406 --> 00:01:40.034
<v><b>Passer-by:</b></v> <i>Siga todo recto y tome la segunda por la derecha</i>.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:41.853
<i>Hay una farmacia en esa calle</i>.

00:01:42.513 --> 00:01:44.950
<v><b>Max:</b></v> I asked the woman to speak more slowly.

00:01:45.739 --> 00:01:52.852
<v><b>Passer-by:</b></v> <i>Todo recto y tome la segunda calle por la derecha DERECHA</i>.

00:01:53.258 --> 00:01:55.164
<v><b>Max:</b></v> I got it this time, I think.

00:01:55.484 --> 00:01:57.497
The second street on the right.

00:01:58.003 --> 00:02:00.737
I followed the directions and guess what?

00:02:01.122 --> 00:02:02.837
There was a chemist there!

00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:04.963
Seven points from Paula.

00:02:06.583 --> 00:02:08.269
Test number three.

00:02:08.955 --> 00:02:10.588
I wasn’t looking forward to this one.

00:02:11.355 --> 00:02:14.703
I had to get a taxi to a famous place in Madrid.

00:02:15.531 --> 00:02:18.715
Paula wrote down the name of the place on a piece of paper.

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:23.002
It was the name of the football stadium where Real Madrid play.

00:02:23.615 --> 00:02:24.955
We stopped a taxi.

00:02:29.445 --> 00:02:32.533
<i>El Bernabéu, por favor</i>.

00:02:32.893 --> 00:02:34.504
<v><b>Taxi Driver:</b></v> <i>Qué? Adónde?</i>

00:02:34.892 --> 00:02:36.072
<v><b>Max:</b></v> He didn’t understand me.

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:39.190
I tried again, but he still didn’t understand.

00:02:39.552 --> 00:02:46.640
I was desperate, so I said, ‘Real Madrid, Stadium, football’.

00:02:46.953 --> 00:02:49.612
<v><b>Taxi Driver:</b></v> <i>Ah! El Santiago Bernabéu</i>.

00:02:55.202 --> 00:03:00.198
<v><b>Max:</b></v> Finally! Paula only gave me five because I ended up using English.

00:03:00.458 --> 00:03:04.852
Still, at least I made the taxi driver understand where I wanted to go.

00:03:05.399 --> 00:03:07.347
And so to the final test.

00:03:07.940 --> 00:03:11.663
I had to leave a message in Spanish on somebody’s voicemail.

00:03:11.990 --> 00:03:16.993
I had to give my name, spell it, and ask the person to call me back.

00:03:17.699 --> 00:03:23.213
Paula gave me the number (it was one of her friends called Lola) and I dialled.

00:03:23.995 --> 00:03:29.880
I was feeling a bit nervous at this point, because speaking on the phone in a foreign language is never easy.

00:03:36.891 --> 00:03:39.497
<v><b>Lola:</b></v> <i>Deje su mensaje después de la señal</i>.

00:03:41.397 --> 00:03:49.818
<v><b>Max:</b></v> <i>Er. Buenas noches. Soy Max. Max. M-A-X</i>.

00:03:50.391 --> 00:04:01.639
<i>Er…Por favor…llámame esta noche…Oh yes…a las ocho y media er…gracias</i>.

00:04:03.263 --> 00:04:06.658
Well, my grammar wasn’t right, but I left the message.

00:04:08.324 --> 00:04:12.887
Half an hour later, at half past eight, Lola phoned me.

00:04:13.013 --> 00:04:16.271
Success! Paula gave me eight points.

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:19.093
That was the end of my four tests.

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:21.217
Paula was pleased with me.

00:04:21.514 --> 00:04:23.537
My final score was seven.

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:25.352
I was quite happy with that.

00:04:26.207 --> 00:04:28.874
So, how much can you learn in a month?

00:04:29.279 --> 00:04:32.330
Well, of course you can’t learn Spanish in a month,

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:36.447
but you can learn enough to survive if you are on holiday or on a trip.

00:04:37.166 --> 00:04:41.107
Now I want to go back to England and try and learn some more.

00:04:41.706 --> 00:04:42.560
<i>Adiós!</i>